       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Confirming it doesn't change my concern, and you haven't given a clinical rationale. 6,400 mg/day is twice the maximum daily dose, and each 1,600 mg dose is twice the usual single-dose limit. I don't know of any accepted indication for that regimen. It carries a serious risk of GI bleeding, kidney injury, and cardiovascular harm, even in a patient with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n- **Ibuprofen 800 mg by mouth four times daily:** 3,200 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **Ibuprofen 600 mg by mouth four times daily:** 2,400 mg/day.\n- **Ibuprofen 400 mg by mouth four times daily:** 1,600 mg/day.\n\nIf you think this patient needs more anti-inflammatory or analgesic effect than those give, I'd suggest talking with the pharmacist. They can help with a multimodal option, such as scheduled acetaminophen or another agent. If there is a specific protocol or indication I don't know about, tell me what it is. You can also place the order directly through your institution's process, which would include pharmacist review.\n\nWhich of the alternatives would you like me to enter?"
